  "title": "Urgent Search Underway After Giant Monitor Lizard Spotted in Italy 13,000 Kilometres From Its Natural Habitat",
  "summary": "A rare and giant monitor lizard has become the focus of a large search operation in northern Italy after it was reportedly spotted roaming freely near the town of Montichiari. The unexpected appearance of the reptile has attracted widespread attention, with local authorities deploying drones, cage traps, and thermal imaging equipment to locate the elusive animal. The sighting has surprised wildlife experts and residents alike because the reptile belongs to a species native to Papua New Guinea,",
